op {
  graph_op_name: "FloorDiv"
  summary: "Returns the element-wise quotient rounded toward negative infinity."
  description: <<END
*NOTE*: `FloorDiv` supports broadcasting. More about broadcasting
[here](http://docs.scipy.org/doc/numpy/user/basics.broadcasting.html)

For floating-point inputs, flooring the computed quotient can differ from
Python's `//` when the divisor is infinite.

For signed integer types, dividing the minimum representable value by `-1`
(e.g. `int_min / -1`) overflows the signed integer range and wraps around to
the minimum signed integer value in two's complement arithmetic rather than
raising an exception.
END
}
